  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(192.357pt, 250.921pt, ". This structural mismatch makes it challenging to form a low-defect ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 277.739pt, "coherent interface, resulting in stress concentration and fracture susceptibility during the ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 304.557pt, "delamination process. Further challenges include oxidation risks during metal film processing. ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 343.079pt, "Due to their antiferromagnetic exchange coupling, ferrimagnets exhibit ultrafast THz spin ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 369.955pt, "dynamics and can be electrically manipulated, making them promising for next-generation ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 396.785pt, "ultrafast information technologies.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.761pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#00b0f0"))
  #line-at(232.271pt, 392.373pt, "28")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(240.064pt, 396.785pt, " As a typical ferrimagnet, CoTb alloys are widely studied in ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 423.602pt, "spintronics for their high spin polarization, strong perpendicular magnetic anisotropy (PMA), and ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 450.478pt, "tunable exchange coupling.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.761pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#00b0f0"))
  #line-at(202.089pt, 446.079pt, "29,30")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.67pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(219.594pt, 450.478pt, " Concurrently, the intrinsic bipolar resistive behavior of CoTb ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 477.238pt, "ferrimagnetic materials enables controllable resistance state modulation in single-device ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 504.055pt, "configurations via spin-orbit torque (SOT) effects—a process that theoretically emulates the ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 530.943pt, "excitatory and inhibitory synaptic weight adjustments in biological systems. This characteristic ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 557.76pt, "positions CoTb as an ideal candidate for realizing single-device positive-negative weight ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 584.578pt, "representation, addressing the limitations of conventional memristors that typically exhibit ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 611.466pt, "unipolar conductance and necessitate differential pair designs (two devices per synapse), thereby ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 638.284pt, "enhancing the efficiency of neural network computations. However, realizing reliable devices ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 665.101pt, "faces challenges in interface control, strain management, and substrate compatibility. Fabricating ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 691.977pt, "freestanding CoTb membranes could overcome these limitations by decoupling material growth ")
  #line-at(70.02pt, 718.795pt, "from device constraints, thereby facilitating optimized synthesis and functional development. ")
]

